{
  "_comment": [
    "Intent rules as DATA, not Python. Adding a new pattern is an edit here,",
    "not a code change and not a redeploy of logic.",
    "",
    "Matching: an intent fires when the description contains at least one word",
    "from `triggers`. `condition` decides between the plain and the conditional",
    "variant of the same verb: 'requires' means the intent only fires when a",
    "condition is present, 'forbids' means it only fires when one is absent,",
    "'ignore' means the condition plays no part.",
    "",
    "A condition is considered present when either a condition word appears in",
    "the description, or a value from the description was found inside one of",
    "the table's sample columns. The second signal is the stronger one: it is",
    "evidence from the user's own data rather than from their phrasing.",
    "",
    "`priority` breaks ties when several intents match; higher wins."
  ],

  "condition_words": [
    "where", "if", "only", "when", "with", "per", "for", "having", "that",
    "unde", "daca", "doar", "numai", "cand", "conditie", "conditii", "care",
    "pentru", "cu", "din care"
  ],

